.jekyll-metadata
# Gemfile.lock is intentionally tracked: ruby/setup-ruby's `bundler-cache: true`
# needs a committed lockfile for deterministic installs. Without it, CI resolves
# dependencies fresh and pulls newer gems (e.g. json 2.21.1) that its restored
# cache lacks -> "Could not find json-x in locally installed gems".

